{{!
    @template theme_dimensions/opengraph

    The Open Graph tags of a public page - a course's enrolment landing page, a
    category's public page or the root of the course index - which a messaging
    app or social network reads when a link to the page is shared. Rendered into
    the document head by the before_standard_head_html_generation hook callback,
    which writes the canonical link beside them and, unless the site is open to
    search engines, a robots noindex directive: the template lint validates a
    fragment as body content, where a meta carrying a name and a canonical link
    are invalid while RDFa property metas are not.

    Every value arrives in the plain spelling and the double stashes escape it
    exactly once for the attribute. The description is optional and comes only
    from text written for the public: a course without a reviewed public
    description gets no description tag at all, never its internal summary. The
    image is optional too, always through the theme's own file route (a
    course's from publicfiles::og_source(), a category's from its branding, the
    root has none); its alt text is the title, and its width and height are
    stated only when the route serves the 1200x630 derivative.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "title": "Pre-hospital Care & Rescue",
        "hasdescription": true,
        "description": "40-hour course for volunteer brigade members.",
        "url": "https://ead.example.org/theme/dimensions/landing.php?id=85",
        "sitename": "Acme",
        "locale": "pt_BR",
        "hasimage": true,
        "imageurl": "https://ead.example.org/pluginfile.php/2611/theme_dimensions/ogimage/85/3f2a9c/og.jpg",
        "imagetype": "image/jpeg",
        "hasimagesize": true,
        "imagewidth": 1200,
        "imageheight": 630
    }
}}
<meta property="og:type" content="website">
<meta property="og:title" content="{{title}}">
{{#hasdescription}}
<meta property="og:description" content="{{description}}">
{{/hasdescription}}
<meta property="og:url" content="{{url}}">
<meta property="og:site_name" content="{{sitename}}">
<meta property="og:locale" content="{{locale}}">
{{#hasimage}}
<meta property="og:image" content="{{imageurl}}">
<meta property="og:image:type" content="{{imagetype}}">
<meta property="og:image:alt" content="{{title}}">
{{#hasimagesize}}
<meta property="og:image:width" content="{{imagewidth}}">
<meta property="og:image:height" content="{{imageheight}}">
{{/hasimagesize}}
{{/hasimage}}
